{
 "about": "Which Dawn of War II unit voices the 3D replay uses (see tools/sim/page/32-view3d-sound.js). 'events' says which of a unit's lines go with what happens in the replay: for each event a list of regular expressions on the game's file names, the first that finds anything being used (looked up separately for each foe race). The game names a line <speaker race><foe race>_<unit>_<situation>_<four 3-letter details>_...: lines for any foe go under the event, lines for one foe race under event.<letter> (s Space Marines, c Chaos, e Eldar, o Orks, t Tyranids, i Guard). 'voices' are the speakers: 'code' is the unit's 3-letter code in the speech archives, or 'dirs' gives a folder in the sound archives and an expression per event (creatures that only growl); 'borrow' names a voice whose lines fill the events this one has none for. 'rules' say which roster entries speak with which voices, first match wins, tested against '<faction> <template> <vehicle> | <kit>' like the models; several voices are shared out among the figures. 'max' is how many lines to keep per event, 'seconds' the longest line taken. Voices with 'dow1' come from Dawn of War: Soulstorm instead, for what Dawn of War II lacks: a unit's folder under sound/speech in Soulstorm's speech archives, whose sub-folders are matched to events by 'events1' (the first listed folder that has anything; a voice may give its own).",
